2. an adapter-first margin boundary that separates SIMM/CRIF or legacy margin calculation from downstream quantum collateral optimization through a normalized MarginRequirement;

3. a higher-order Pauli Hamiltonian formulation for local collateral reallocation;

4. a one-sided coverage slack ladder that distinguishes unacceptable margin shortfall from operationally acceptable surplus;

5. collateral-specific constraint-preserving mixers for one-hot eligibility groups, movement-cardinality budgets, side-preserving VM/IM allocation, and substitution pairs;

6. a warm-started HO-QAOA workflow for active-neighborhood optimization under near-term quantum limits;

